G0622.def:
**ἀπ-όλλυμι and ἀπολλύω **
[in LXX for אָבַד, etc. (38 words in all)].
1. Act.,
1 **to destroy utterly, destroy, kill**: Mk 124, 922, al.; τ. ψνχήν, [[Mat.10.28|Mat.10:28]], al.;
2 **to lose utterly**: [[Mat.10.42|Mat.10:42]], al.; metaphorically, of failing to save, [[Jhn.6.39; 18.9|Jhn.6:39 18:9]].
2. Mid.,
1 **to perish**;
(a) **of things**: [[Mat.5.29|Mat.5:29]], [[Jhn.6.12|Jhn.6:12]], [[Heb.1.11|Heb.1:11]] (LXX, al.;
(b) **of persons**: [[Mat.8.26|Mat.8:26]], al. Metaphorical, of loss of eternal life, [[Jhn.3.15-16; 10.28; 17.12|Jhn.3:15-16 10:28 17:12]], [[Rom.2.12|Rom.2:12]], [[1Co.8.11; 15.18|1Co.8:11 15:18]], [[2Pe.3.9|2Pe.3:9]]. In οἱ ἀπολλὺμενοι, the perishing, contrasted in [[1Co.1.18|1Co.1:18]], al., with οἱ σωζόμενοι, the "perfective" force of the verb, WH. " implies the completion of the process of destruction," is illustrated (see M, _Pr._, 114 f.; M, _Th._, ii, 2:10);
2 **to be lost**: [[Luk.15.4; 21.18|Luk.15:4 21:18]]. Metaphorical, on the basis of the relation between shepherd and flock, of spiritual destitution and alienation from God: [[Mat.10.6; 15.24|Mat.10:6 15:24]], [[Luk.19.10|Luk.19:10]] (MM, see word; _DCG_, i, 191 f., ii, 76, 554; Cremer, 451)
(AS)

G0649.def:
**ἀπο-στέλλω**,
[in LXX very freq., almost always for שׁלח ;]
prop., **to send away, to dispatch** on service;
1. **to send** with a commission, or on service;
(a) **of persons**: Christ, [[Mat.10.40|Mat.10:40]] the apostles, 10:16; servants, [[Mrk.12.2|Mrk.12:2]] angels, 13:27;
(b) **of things**: ὄνος, [[Mat.21.3|Mat.21:3]] τὸ δρέπανον, [[Mrk.4.29|Mrk.4:29]] τ. λόγον, [[Act.10.36|Act.10:36]] τ. ἐπαγγελίαν (i.e. the promised Holy Spirit), [[Luk.24.49|Luk.24:49]], Rec.; before εἰς, [[Mat.20.2|Mat.20:2]], [[Luk.11.49|Luk.11:49]], [[Jhn.3.17|Jhn.3:17]]; ὀπίσω, [[Luk.19.14|Luk.19:14]] ἔμπροσθεν, [[Jhn.3.28|Jhn.3:28]] πρὸ προσώπου, [[Mat.11.10|Mat.11:10]] πρός, [[Mat.21.34|Mat.21:34]] with ref. to sender or place of departure: ἀπό, [[Luk.1.26|Luk.1:26]] (Rec. ὑπό); παρά, [[Jhn.1.6|Jhn.1:6]] ἐκ, [[Jhn.1.19|ib. 1:19]]; ὑπό, [[Act.10.17|Act.10:17]] (Rec. ἀπό); before inf., [[Mrk.3.14|Mrk.3:14]], al.; ἵνα, [[Mrk.12.2|Mrk.12:2]], al.; εἰς (of purpose), [[Heb.1.14|Heb.1:14]] without direct obj.: before πρός, [[Jhn.5.33|Jhn.5:33]] λέγων, [[Jhn.11.3|Jhn.11:3]] ἀποστείλας, with indic., [[Mat.2.16|Mat.2:16]], [[Act.7.14|Act.7:14]], [[Rev.1.1|Rev.1:1]].
2. **to send away, dismiss**: [[Luk.4.18|Luk.4:18]], [[Mrk.5.10; 8.26; 12.3|Mrk.5:10 8:26 12:3]] (cf. ἐξ-, συν-αποστέλλω).
_SYN._: πέμπω, the general term. ἀ. "suggests official or authoritative sending" (see Thayer, see word πέμπω; Westc., _Jo._, 298; _Epp. Jo._, 125; Cremer, 529; MM, see word). (AS)
